{"id": "sevt_019L8goZfNSxwAtpZ2PbPbFe", "content": [{"text": "**Root cause is `371dfe2`, not the catalog cache change.** Its refactor turned one batched `order_items` query into a per-order query, and the resulting N+1 pattern saturated the checkout DB connection pool.\n\n**Deploy timeline vs. metrics (checkout)**\n- 14:03:53 commit `371dfe2` (alice, \"refactor order summary builder for readability\"). Deployed 14:06:20. p99 leaves its baseline (~75 ms) at 14:06 (101 ms) and climbs steadily from there.\n- 14:15:43 commit `db46df5` (carol, \"temporarily disable catalog cache\"). Deployed 14:18:10, rolled back 14:23:40. p99 keeps rising after the rollback, so this change did not drive the spike.\n- p99 jumps from 412 ms at 14:28 to 2152 ms at 14:29 and reaches ~3.7 s by 14:30.\n- `db_pool_utilization` rises from ~0.17 at 14:00 to 1.0 at 14:38, where it stays pinned.\n\n**Diff evidence (`371dfe2`)**\n- Removed: one `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=ids)` query, grouped in memory.\n- Added: a loop that runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.order_id)` once per open order. This is the \"per-row query where there used to be a batch\" pattern on the runbook list.\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- Of the `order_items` queries in the log, 3,770 are per-row `order_id = ?` and 23 are the batched `IN (?)` form. All are in the 14:xx hour.\n- From 14:38 the log shows `DB connection pool exhausted (active=50/50, waiters=12)` with `PoolTimeout` 500s on `/api/checkout/summary` and `/api/checkout/validate`, with latencies around 4 s.\n\n**Open questions**\n- The 14:29 step (412 \u2192 2152 ms in one minute) is steeper than the gradual climb from 14:06 that the refactor alone would predict. I did not find a deploy that explains it. The likely reason is that the pool was near saturation by then and queueing amplified the latency, but I have not verified that.\n- I did not check `cart`, `auth`, `inventory`, or upstream dependencies, since the deploy evidence already explains the spike.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Revert `371dfe2` or restore the batched query and in-memory grouping. Then confirm `db_pool_utilization` and checkout p99 recover.\n\n**Root cause:** `371dfe2` \u2014 the refactor replaced the batched `order_items` lookup with a per-order query, so each checkout summary issues N extra queries that exhaust the 50-connection DB pool and push p99 to several seconds.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T11:49:35.175434Z", "type": "agent.message"}
